<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<document level="portable" type="default">

  <documentinfo>
    <uri docid="home" title="Berlioz Admin development application"/>
  </documentinfo>

  <section id="title">
    <fragment id="intro">
      <heading level="1">Berlioz Admin development application</heading>
      <para>This is a small Berlioz application used to develop and try
        <link href="/bzadmin/config.html">Berlioz Admin</link>, the admin overlay deployed with a Berlioz
        application at <monospace>/bzadmin/*</monospace>. It plays the part of the host: it is not distributed,
        and everything here only exists to give the admin pages something to show.</para>
    </fragment>
  </section>

  <section id="content">

    <fragment id="access">
      <heading level="2">Access</heading>
      <para>A host authenticates its users and maps the admin filter after its authentication. Here,
        <monospace>LocalAdminAccessFilter</monospace> grants admin access to requests from this machine only.
        A real host uses its own authentication, container roles or the fallback login: see
        <monospace>docs/access.md</monospace>.</para>
    </fragment>

    <fragment id="caches">
      <heading level="2">Caches</heading>
      <para>The admin pages never create a cache: they show those of the application. This application has
        three cache managers, one per supported library:</para>
      <list>
        <item><bold>EHCache 2</bold>, the default manager from <monospace>ehcache.xml</monospace>:
          <monospace>static-web-caching</monospace> and <monospace>PSML</monospace>.</item>
        <item><bold>EHCache 3</bold> through JCache, registered as <monospace>dev-ehcache3</monospace>:
          <monospace>static-files</monospace>.</item>
        <item><bold>Caffeine</bold> through JCache, registered as <monospace>dev-caffeine</monospace>:
          <monospace>static-files</monospace>.</item>
      </list>
      <para>Each static file (scripts, styles, fonts) is looked up and stored in the static file cache of every
        library, so their statistics and configuration can be compared for the same requests. This page is
        read through the <monospace>PSML</monospace> cache: reload it to count a hit, or edit
        <monospace>WEB-INF/psml/content/home.psml</monospace> to replace the entry.</para>
      <para>See the <link href="/bzadmin/cache.html">Cache</link> page.</para>
    </fragment>

    <fragment id="sections">
      <heading level="2">What to look at</heading>
      <list>
        <item><link href="/bzadmin/config.html">Config</link>: the global configuration of
          <monospace>config-local.xml</monospace>, with sample application properties and secrets that are
          redacted.</item>
        <item><link href="/bzadmin/services.html">Services</link>: the services of this application
          (<monospace>default</monospace> group) and of the overlay.</item>
        <item><link href="/bzadmin/files.html">PSML</link>: the documents of <monospace>WEB-INF/psml</monospace>,
          including this one.</item>
        <item><link href="/bzadmin/xslt.html">XSLT</link>: <monospace>default.xsl</monospace>, the stylesheet of
          this page, and those of the overlay.</item>
        <item><link href="/bzadmin/logs.html">Logs</link>, <link href="/bzadmin/application.html">Application</link>
          and <link href="/bzadmin/system.html">System</link>: the logs, versions and runtime of this
          server.</item>
      </list>
    </fragment>

  </section>

</document>
